        "caption": "Drew by Robert Home, on his visit to Dhaka in 1799. The initial drawings were executed from a boat or barge moored at a vantage point in midstream of the Buriganga River and, later on, painted in oils. The painting shows the river either at high tide or during the monsoon floods. This painting also shows the growth of invasive wild vegetation at various points of the fort.",
